# CONSTRAINT RULES

Database constraints must enforce invariants that must always be true.

Use:
- PK for identity;
- FK for relationships;
- UNIQUE for business uniqueness;
- CHECK for finite/domain-valid values;
- NOT NULL for required data.

Do not rely solely on UI validation.

Do not add a constraint that contradicts an approved business rule.

Before changing a constraint:
- inspect existing data;
- identify violations;
- define remediation;
- assess production impact;
- migrate safely.
